{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1154600-you-re-entering-another-dimension","id":1154600,"title":"You're Entering Another Dimension...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-31T20:48:39-07:00","id":1154600,"title":"You're Entering Another Dimension...","content":"So as I marathon the original Twilight Zone on Halloween Night, let's throw this one out. How CoD is the Twilight Zone for you guys?<br /> <br /> For me, here are my favorite candidates. Yes, it is a long list. Which episodes do you think are CoD material, and which ones that I didn't touch do you think deserve to be included?<br /> <br /> <i><u><b>DO NOT SPOIL ANYTHING FOR THOSE WHO HAVEN'T SEEN!!!</b></u></i><br /> <br /> <b>The Sixteen-Millimeter Shrine:</b> When an aging film star realizes how time has passed by, she realizes sometimes life is all in pictures...<br /> <br /> <b>And When the Sky Was Opened:</b> Three men in an experimental aircraft come back as heroes, if only they could remember what happened...<br /> <br /> <b>What You Need:</b> A mysterious peddler makes his rounds, and a small-time hood finds out what he wants isn't what he needs...<br /> <br /> <b>The Four of Us Are Dying:</b> A con artist with the ability to change his face finds out exactly what happens when you play with another's life.<br /> <br /> <b>The Fever:</b> An old man finds out that one way or another, the house always wins...<br /> <br /> <b>The Last Flight:</b> When a pilot in an antiquated biplane lands on a US Air Force base, more questions are raised than answers.<br /> <br /> <b>The Monsters Are Due On Maple Street:</b> Who are the real monsters when the community of Maple Street finds out that they are not alone?<br /> <br /> <b>Long Live Walter Jameson:</b> A masterful history teacher is confronted by his own past...<br /> <br /> <b>The After Hours:</b> A woman is driven to the brink of madness when she simply goes out to by a scarf...<br /> <br /> <b>The Mighty Casey:</b> The down-and-out Hoboken Zephyrs find that new player Casey is better for a reason...<br /> <br /> <b>The Man in the Bottle:</b> A couple finds out that every wish has a consequence...<br /> <br /> <b>A Thing About Machines:</b> Mr. Finchley finds out that even the lifeless have standards...<br /> <br /> <b>The Howling Man:</b> Some things, and some men, need to stay locked up for a reason...<br /> <br /> <b>A Most Unusual Camera:</b> A group of small-time hoods find out that the future is a dangerous thing...<br /> <br /> <b>A Penny For Your Thoughts:</b> When a meek man gains a special gift, life can change on the flip of a coin...<br /> <br /> <b>The Prime Mover:</b> A gambler and his telekinetic friend go on a journey through what makes a monster...<br /> <br /> <b>Long-Distance Call:</b> When a toy phone becomes a conduit to death, how can a mother and father save their son?<br /> <br /> <b>Will The Real Martian Please Stand Up:</b> A group of stranded travelers and cops are forced to ask who is who in the snowy back roads of New England...<br /> <br /> <b>A Game of Pool:</b> A small time pool shark challenges one of the greatest to a game of life and death...<br /> <br /> <b>The Mirror:</b> A revolutionary-turned-dictator is haunted by signs of impending betrayal just behind him...<br /> <br /> <b>Deaths-Head Revisited:</b> Mr. &quot;Schmidt&quot; returns to the small town Dachau, Germany, where the past has been waiting for him...<br /> <br /> <b>Kick The Can:</b> Childhood is just a state of mind, or is it something more...<br /> <br /> <b>The Jungle:</b> A harried executive is haunted by threats from the construction of his company's dam in the Congo...<br /> <br /> <b>Little Girl Lost:</b> A little girl vanishes from her bedroom, and her parents are forced to take a leap of faith...<br /> <br /> <b>The Dummy:</b> A sad little ventriloquist gets more than he bargained for with a new dummy...<br /> <br /> <b>Young Man's Fancy:</b> A husband and wife are faced with ghosts of the past in the home of the husband's mother...<br /> <br /> <b>The Thirty-Fathom Grave:</b> A chief petty officer is forced to confront the ghosts of the war and his own guilt...<br /> <br /> <b>He's Alive:</b> A pathetic little man who wants more gets exactly what he bargained for...<br /> <br /> <b>Miniature:</b> What happens when a man becomes obsessed with a small museum piece others pass by without noticing...<br /> <br /> <b>Printer's Devil:</b> A failing newspaper man becomes forced into a desperate bid to save his business...<br /> <br /> <b>The New Exhibit:</b> Who is guilty when murders start to occur when a series of wax figures are left alone?<br /> <br /> <b>The Parallel:</b> Which side is which as an astronaut tries to puzzle out where on Earth he landed?<br /> <br /> <b>Steel:</b> A manager and his aged fighting robot are faced with one last bout...<br /> <br /> <b>Living Doll: </b>Her name is Talking Tina, and she doesn't like you...<br /> <br /> <b>Uncle Simon:</b> A young woman is forced to realize just what money can make a person live through...<br /> <br /> <b>A Short Drink From A Certain Fountain:</b> One man is willing to do anything for his wife, til death do they part...<br /> <br /> <b>Number 12 Looks Just Like You:</b> Is there any room for life when individuality is wiped away?<br /> <br /> <b>Black Leather Jackets:</b> Maybe, love doesn't conquer all...<br /> <br /> <b>From Agnes-With Love:</b> Robots might not dream of electric sheep, but they may just feel more than electric current in their wires...<br /> <br /> <b>Queen of the Nile:</b> Beauty may be skin deep, but life is timeless...<br /> <br /> <b>The Masks:</b> When an old patriarch finally is ready to pass, his inheritors find out just what their flaws will cost them...<br /> <br /> <b>The Encounter:</b> Two men, one attic, one relic of war...<br /> <br /> <b>Mr. Garrity and the Graves:</b> When a con man rides in promising to bring the dead back to life, a Western town finds out that some things should stay buried...<br /> <br /> <b>The Brain Center At Whipples:</b> Mr. Whipple believes in efficiency, and he'll soon find out the cost...<br /> <br /> <b>The Fear:</b> What do we call it when we're faced with that which defies all belief?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T22:24:03-07:00","id":1154622,"title":"","content":"<b>One For the Angels:</b> An anachronistic sidewalk pitchman grapples with the inevitability of obsolescence and mortality, only to rediscover purpose in its embrace.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lateness of the Hour:</b> What is identity but a self image derived from memories and relationships? If those memories and relationships can be fabricated and programmed, what separates us from machines?<br /> <br /> <b>Nick of Time:</b> A couple look into their future and don't like the forecast. Superstition can be powerful in the face of uncertainty and randomness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 11-01-2017, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}